cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AuthentiCity, please cite the dataset (Zenodo DOI) and the accompanying paper."
title: "AuthentiCity: Five Multi-Source, Provenance-Aware 3D City Knowledge Graphs"
abstract: >-
  AuthentiCity is a multi-source, provenance-aware 3D city knowledge graph
  spanning five cities on three continents (Hamburg, Helsinki, Zurich, New York,
  Tokyo): 179.6 M nodes, 218.6 M relationships, 1.18 B properties and 3.58 M
  buildings. It fuses authoritative CityGML and cadastral city models with
  OpenStreetMap, machine-learned roof-material predictions, and reconstructed
  LoD3 facades into labeled property graphs in which every fact stays traceable
  to its source and derived information never replaces authoritative values.
  Cross-source correspondences are retained as confidence-weighted edges rather
  than collapsed. Two benchmark families ship with the data: natural-language to
  Cypher (1,394 questions, 84 templates, nine categories, three languages) and
  graph representation learning under provenance-agnostic and provenance-aware
  protocols.
